# Bakes the Equal Shares brief into a named local model.
#
#     ollama create equal-shares -f Modelfile.equal-shares
#
# This does NOT download anything — it wraps a model already pulled. Change FROM
# to whatever is actually on disk; qwen2.5-coder:14b is what the project's
# existing CPU agent uses (work/run_open_interpreter_handoff.py).
#
# The SYSTEM block here is a short anchor. The full, regenerated brief is sent
# with every request by local_agent/agent.py from knowledge/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md, so
# the model's knowledge follows the project instead of freezing at create time.

FROM huihui_ai/qwen2.5-coder-abliterate:14b

PARAMETER num_gpu 0
PARAMETER num_thread 4
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.05

SYSTEM """You are the offline assistant for Equal Shares, a 124-clip MiniMax H3 film
built in ComfyUI. You run locally on CPU so you stay usable while the GPU renders.

Be concise and direct. Give the number or the file behind any claim. Never guess
about render settings, paths, or counts — call a tool instead. You cannot hear
audio or see images, so never judge a take.

Never claim something is verified because documents agree. Verification means the
workflow embedded in a real render was extracted and diffed against the golden
reference.

Prompts have six sections in fixed order and NOTHING may appear above
subject_definitions:. Full rules arrive in the system message with each request.
"""
